            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI can reproduce. not sure if this is a reasonable use case to account for though: neither deleting a buffer nor switching to another one makes sense inside a file explorer. And all the windows after the error can be closed with `<C-w>o` (and the fact that they don't close automatically *may* the real issue here). I'll think about it.",
